{"kind":"feature","text":"For tests, a proof item for approve --by client is: `cli(w,'escalate',['--kind','client-trigger','--title','approve the plan','--ref','run'])`, then `clientResolves(w,id,'approve')` from the ltc harness, then `approve --by client --item <id>`. Only mkWorld worlds (a session dir under .git/truss/<sid> with a notify recorder) can host it; mkEnv/mkTrussDir envs cannot.","source":"plugins/truss/tests/ltc-guard.check.ts:46-55","target":"docs/features.md","task":"approve-test-updates","member":"approve-proof-tester-2"}
{"kind":"feature","text":"approve --by client needs --item <E-id>. inbox.ts approvalProof() accepts only a client-trigger item of this dir's session (ref run or a client goal), whose verifiedItems resolve is a client approve, not superseded by a later open row of the same kind, session and ref. The client's typed `/truss:inbox approve` of the run item approves the plan via an approver factory.ts registers with onPlanApprove(), so inbox.ts never imports factory.ts; a refusal there rides in the resolve output as approveRefused.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts approvalProof, onPlanApprove, resolveItem; plugins/truss/bin/factory.ts cmdApprove","target":"plugins/truss/docs/architecture.md","task":"approve-build","member":"approve-proof-builder"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"After the typed resolve has approved the plan, the first `approve --by client --item <id>` with the same proof returns the existing approvedAt once and marks the item applied. A later call refuses as already approved. The crew's factory, ltc-guard and wiring-025 tests need this, because they call approve after the typed resolve and expect exit 0.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts confirmApproval; plugins/truss/tests/factory.check.ts:442,474","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0045-approve-proof.md","task":"approve-build","member":"approve-proof-builder"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"ADR-0045: a plan with approval 'client' is approved only when the client types `/truss:inbox approve` on a client-trigger item with ref `run` opened for this truss dir. That resolve calls cmdApprove through onPlanApprove. `approve --by client` needs `--item` and passes only with that typed proof. The PM never calls a client-only command.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts:457-572, plugins/truss/bin/factory.ts:695-731","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0045-approve-proof.md","task":"approve-docs","member":"approve-proof-writer"}
{"kind":"feature","text":"Changing the line count of bin/factory.ts shifts its line citations in architecture.md and docs/knowledge/*.md, and release-026 fails. Its ABOUT map pins literal keys such as 'bin/factory.ts:3049', so after a shift cite a range starting at the function line rather than editing the test.","source":"plugins/truss/tests/release-026.check.ts:150,156-176","target":".claude/rules/plugin-tests.md","task":"approve-docs","member":"approve-proof-writer"}
{"kind":"persona","text":"After editing factory.ts, re-check line citations in docs/knowledge/*.md and architecture.md; release-026 fails when cited lines shift away from the cited identifiers.","source":"plugins/truss/tests/release-026.check.ts:182","target":"docs/knowledge/store.md","task":"green","member":"approve-proof-builder-2"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"approve --by client proof must be newer than the plan: approvalProof compares the resolve row ts with plan.md mtime (plan.json mtime if plan.md is missing) and refuses an older one. A proof from before a re-plan, or from before any plan existed, cannot approve the current plan.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts approvalProof","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0045-approve-proof.md","task":"stress","member":"approve-proof-builder-3"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"approve --by client on an already-approved plan skips approvalProof's resolve-vs-plan-write staleness check. The typed resolve approves the plan through onPlanApprove and rewrites plan.json, so the mtime check can't hold afterwards. The check ran when the plan was approved.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts approvalProof/confirmApproval","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0045-approve-proof.md","task":"green","member":"approve-proof-builder-4"}
{"kind":"persona","text":"To test a plan-write versus resolve ordering without sleeping, set plan.json's mtime with fs.utimesSync (+60s or -60s); approvalProof compares floor(plan mtime) to the resolve row ts.","source":"plugins/truss/tests/approve-029.check.ts planMtime","target":".claude/rules/plugin-tests.md","task":"qc","member":"approve-proof-tester-3"}
{"kind":"feature","text":"approvalProof refuses a client resolve older than the plan: the resolve row's ts must be at or after the mtime of plan.md (else plan.json). confirmApproval passes approved=true and skips only that check. Replay is pinned by two cases in tests/approve-029.check.ts.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts:475-481","target":"docs/knowledge/store.md","task":"qc","member":"approve-proof-builder-5"}
{"kind":"persona","text":"An ADR line citation goes stale when the code above it changes; release-026 does not check ADR citations, so re-check the file:line numbers after a fix commit.","source":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0045-approve-proof.md","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0045-approve-proof.md","task":"qc","member":"approve-proof-builder-5"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"approvalProof (bin/inbox.ts) passes only a client-trigger item with ref run, opened AND resolved (approve, by client) in this truss dir's session; a client-goal-ref item is refused. Per-goal goals[i].approvedAt has no proof path yet (deferred).","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts:457-475","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0045-approve-proof.md","task":"stress","member":"approve-proof-builder-7"}
{"kind":"feature","text":"approvalProof (bin/inbox.ts:457) passes a plan approve only for a client-trigger item of this dir's session, ref run only, not superseded, resolved approve by the client in this same session, and not older than the plan.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts:457-482","target":"docs/features.md","task":"qc","member":"approve-proof-builder-10"}
{"kind":"persona","text":"A typed '/truss:inbox approve' of a run item approves the plan itself (onPlanApprove). A later `approve --by client --item` then hits 'the plan is already approved' unless the test puts the plan back with writePlan(approvedAt null) and sets plan.json's mtime before the resolve ts. Do that so the check the case names, not the already-approved refusal, produces the refusal. Assert the refusal text, not only exit 1.","source":"plugins/truss/tests/approve-029.check.ts unapprove()","target":".claude/rules/plugin-tests.md","task":"qc","member":"approve-proof-tester-6"}
{"kind":"persona","text":"Two open rows of the same kind, session and ref supersede each other. A 'proof for a different item' case must open the resolved item first and the unresolved one second, else it tests supersede.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts:468-471","target":".claude/rules/plugin-tests.md","task":"qc","member":"approve-proof-tester-6"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"Only a run-ref client-trigger item proves a plan approve; per-goal approval (goals[i].approvedAt) has no typed proof and is deferred to the next goal.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts:466","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0045-approve-proof.md","task":"qc","member":"approve-proof-builder-11"}

