{"kind":"feature","text":"factory.ts requires crew slugs to match SLUG (lowercase); admit/start need a plan.json in the session dir; resolve --by pm is refused with `<kind> is resolved by the client, not by pm` before the code is checked, so a refusal test needs no real client code.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/factory.ts:3594, plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts:480","target":"docs/features.md","task":"cli-tests","member":"crew-decisions-tester"}
{"kind":"feature","text":"Real factory escalate dedupes on kind+ref while an item is open (a second escalate with the same --ref links the crew and returns deduped:true, code ''); the inbox listing row has {id,kind,crews,ref,blocking,state,decision,by,note}. A crew-call wait can therefore escalate again on resume and re-read through `inbox --kind <kind> --crew <slug>` without opening a second item.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts:316-326, plugins/truss/bin/inbox.ts:549-557","target":"docs/knowledge/inbox.md","task":"stage-tests","member":"crew-decisions-tester-2"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"A crew product call's inbox ref is crew-call:<slug>:<task>@<truss dir path under .git/truss>[@<plan approvedAt>]. factory inbox and escalate dedupe span sessions, so the run key keeps an older or other session's item with the same slug and task from answering or swallowing this run's call. The stage reads approvedAt from args.truss.approvedAt, which bin/factory.ts:1362 does not pass yet.","source":"plugins/truss/workflows/stage.js:1005 (RUN_KEY, callRef, callAt)","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0033-crew-knowledge-and-product-calls.md","task":"stage-wait","member":"crew-decisions-builder-3"}
