{"kind":"decision","text":"The 5.5-family pricing in .claude/truss.json uses 1.25x input for cache write 5m and 2x input for 1h (claude-api skill, shared/prompt-caching.md economics), and the skill lists no per-model write price. Cache read is 0.05x for Opus 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5, and the Haiku 5.5 value of $0.01 is derived from the general 0.1x rule. Haiku 5.5 has a >100K-token prompt tier that the flat pricing shape cannot express.","source":".claude/truss.json; claude-api skill shared/prompt-caching.md line 144; SKILL.md Current Models table","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0038-cost-budgets-and-ledger.md","task":"pricing-55","member":"hygiene-builder"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"citationFailures (release-026.check.ts) accepts a citation when a symbol named in its clause appears anywhere in the cited file, and it skips bare `:N` follow-on citations. So a drifted line number never fails release-026 or hygiene-029. To find drift, check that the cited lines themselves hold the symbol.","source":"plugins/truss/tests/release-026.check.ts:160,177","task":"doc-citations","member":"hygiene-writer"}
{"kind":"persona","text":"release-026's tolerant citation check passes a citation whose symbol is anywhere in the file, so a stale line number cannot be caught by it. A fix that depends on exact lines needs its own case that reads the line numbers directly, as hygiene-029.check.ts does for retro SKILL.md.","source":"plugins/truss/tests/hygiene-029.check.ts:137","target":".claude/rules/plugin-tests.md","task":"qc","member":"hygiene-tester-5"}
{"kind":"product","text":"The Haiku 5.5 prompt tier over 100K tokens is expressed in `.claude/truss.json` as `claude-haiku-5-5.longContext {abovePromptTokens: 100000}` and priced in bin/cost.ts. The product-decisions Pricing line that calls it inexpressible is stale and is pinned red by hygiene-029.check.ts.","source":"docs/knowledge/product-decisions.md:41","target":"docs/knowledge/product-decisions.md","task":"qc","member":"hygiene-tester-5"}
