{"kind":"feature","text":"Crew finisher lease in bin/store.ts: takeLease(dir, name, opts) creates <dir>/locks/<name>.lease with createExclusive ({pid, host, since, refreshed, token}) and returns {token} or null while a live lease holds. refreshLease(dir, name, token, opts) returns a boolean; releaseLease(dir, name, token, opts) removes only its own lease. LEASE_STALE_MS is 300000 and LEASE_REFRESH_MS is 30000. A stale lease is removed under the <name>.lease.break mutex with a token re-check. A removal that fails on win32 (EPERM or EACCES) returns null, and a later call recovers the lease.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/store.ts:391-515","target":"docs/knowledge/store.md","task":"store-lease","member":"resume-guard-builder-3"}
{"kind":"feature","text":"finish and start --resume hold a lease named finisher-<slug> (store.ts takeLease/refreshLease/releaseLease). finish takes it per crew before writing, refreshes it before each merge and releases it in a finally. start --resume takes it before ensureWorktree and merges the target via mergeIn; on a conflict it runs git merge --abort and puts syncConflicts: [paths] on the crew entry instead of refusing.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/factory.ts cmdFinish/finishRun/cmdStartResume","target":"docs/features.md","task":"factory-guard","member":"resume-guard-builder-4"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"Finisher lease: D/locks/finisher-<slug>.lease, a file (not a lock dir) taken by store.ts takeLease. It goes stale when the same host's pid is dead or it is older than LEASE_STALE_MS (300 s); a lease from another host is judged by age only. LEASE_REFRESH_MS (30 s) has no timer caller, and finish refreshes only before each crew's merge. start --resume holds the lease only while the command runs.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/store.ts:391-516; plugins/truss/bin/factory.ts:2026-2079, :3220-3261, :3334","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0047-resume-guard.md","task":"adr-docs","member":"resume-guard-writer"}
{"kind":"persona","text":"A multi-process lease race test must keep every worker alive until all have finished: an exited holder's same-host lease is dead-pid stale and takeLease rightly lets another process take it, which looks like a double grant. Spawned worker scripts read their args from process.argv.slice(2), not slice(1); slice(1) makes a self-import that hangs on top-level await. Give such tests a { timeout } so a worker failure fails the case instead of hanging the stage.","source":"plugins/truss/tests/resume-029.check.ts:144-179","target":".claude/rules/plugin-tests.md","task":"green","member":"resume-guard-tester-3"}
{"kind":"persona","text":"Any change that adds or removes lines in bin/factory.ts or bin/store.ts shifts the line citations in plugins/truss/docs/architecture.md and docs/knowledge/*.md. release-026.check.ts line 196 checks that every cited range still holds one of the named symbols. Re-run `node --test plugins/truss/tests/release-026.check.ts` after such a change and re-point the stale citations.","source":"plugins/truss/tests/release-026.check.ts:164","target":".claude/rules/plugin-tests.md","task":"green","member":"resume-guard-builder-9"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"`cmdSync` and `cmdStartResume` follow ADR-0026 item 58: with a merge, rebase, cherry-pick or revert in progress in the crew worktree, neither merges into nor aborts it. `sync` refuses with `{merged:false, conflicts, inProgress, why}` and stage.js `syncStep` sends that to the resolver. Resume records the unmerged paths as `syncConflicts`.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/factory.ts cmdSync, cmdStartResume","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0047-resume-guard.md","task":"stress","member":"resume-guard-builder-10"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"A finisher lease cannot be kept fresh while `mergeCrew` blocks in `spawnSync` (the acceptance test). `mergeCrew(..., leaseToken)` re-checks it with `refreshLease` before moving the target and refuses with 'finisher lease lost' when the token is gone. Open gap: another finisher can still run git in the same worktree during that window.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/factory.ts mergeCrew, finishRun","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0047-resume-guard.md","task":"stress","member":"resume-guard-builder-10"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"A same-host lease is stale only when its pid is dead, because the finisher blocks in spawnSync during the acceptance test and cannot refresh. Another host's lease goes stale after LEASE_STALE_MS (300 s) with no refresh.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/store.ts takeLease","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0047-resume-guard.md","task":"qc","member":"resume-guard-builder-11"}
{"kind":"persona","text":"Keep `.claude/rules/*.md` at or under 40 total lines, front matter included. Merge bullets rather than add lines. After a change to a knowledge doc's sources, re-stamp `verified` with the sha of the commit that changed the sources, then run `factory.ts knowledge-lint`.","source":"factory.ts knowledge-lint over-budget and stale findings","target":".claude/rules/plugin-tests.md","task":"qc","member":"resume-guard-builder-11"}
{"kind":"feature","text":"cmdSync (factory.ts:984) refuses with {merged:false, conflicts, inProgress, why} (exit 1) while a merge or other operation is in progress in the crew worktree. cmdStartResume (about :2055) never merges into or aborts such an operation. It answers the unmerged paths as entry.syncConflicts, which go to the resolver.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/factory.ts:984-993, 2052-2056; tests sync 1/sync 2 in plugins/truss/tests/factory-fixes4-resume.check.ts","target":"docs/features.md","task":"qc","member":"resume-guard-tester-5"}
{"kind":"decision","text":"Same-host finisher leases are judged by pid liveness alone, never by age. A reused pid can wedge a crew's finish and start --resume with `finisher live` until locks/finisher-<slug>.lease is deleted by hand. Fixing it needs a process start time recorded in the lease.","source":"plugins/truss/bin/store.ts:483","target":"plugins/truss/docs/adr/0047-resume-guard.md","task":"qc","member":"resume-guard-builder-12"}
{"kind":"persona","text":"release-026 line-citation check verifies only that a cited line exists, not that it covers the claim. After editing factory.ts or store.ts, re-check every file:line citation in architecture.md and the ADRs by hand.","source":"plugins/truss/tests/release-026.check.ts (every line citation test)","target":".claude/rules/plugin-tests.md","task":"qc","member":"resume-guard-builder-12"}

